<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Transleithania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was a central European kingdom ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> from the sixteenth century onwards. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> it became an equal partner in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Dual Monarchy</a>, governing its half of the state, known as Transleithania, with its own parliament. This settlement created the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Hungary" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(1915-1918;_angels).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…I. The title gave a common name to the composite monarchy the Habsburgs had built since the sixteenth century: the Austrian hereditary lands, the Lands of the Bohemian Crown, the <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> with Croatia, the Grand Principality of Transylvania, and Galicia, taken in the partitions of Poland.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…states, the Austrian half officially styled &quot;the Kingdoms and Lands represented in the Imperial Council&quot; (Cisleithania) and the <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> (Transleithania), sharing a single monarch, crowned King of Hungary in Budapest in June 1867, a joint foreign ministry, a common army and common finances for these joint…</blockquote><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> was created by the conversion of the Magyar principality that had occupied the Carpathian basin from about 895.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1000-1301">Kingdom of Hungary (1000-1301) · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> had been founded around 1000, when Stephen I of the Árpád dynasty was crowned its first Christian king.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Wallachia fought first the <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> and then, for four centuries, the Ottoman Empire, as enemy or vassal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-wallachia">Principality of Wallachia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Latin remained the official language of the <b>Kingdom of Hungary</b> until 1844, when the Hungarian diet made Hungarian the language of government in its place.</blockquote><a href="/language/latin">Latin · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
